                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Stam, John C./64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-14T18:00:00-05:00">February 14, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Your 69, February 9, 10 a.m. and 73, February 13, 11 a.m. Department approves
                    proposed action by the Legation outlined in antepenultimate and penultimate
                    paragraphs of latter telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
